Description: CVE-2026-82560 - Fix infinite loop in Pod::Text wrap() with pathological margins
 Pod::Text and its subclasses (Color, Overstrike, Termcap) compute the
 available wrapping width as opt_width minus the current MARGIN.  When a
 document requests an indentation (via nested =over) that is greater than or
 equal to the configured output width, the resulting $width becomes zero or
 negative.  The wrapping loop "while (length > $width)" then never makes
 progress because the regular expressions can match zero characters, causing
 an infinite loop (CWE-835) and a denial of service when formatting untrusted
 POD input.
 .
 This backports the security-relevant portion of podlators v6.1.1
 (upstream commit 70510174f69eb54aa6d617bde4e1402cd9b7c61f, "Handle
 pathological margins in Pod::Text"): each wrap() implementation now detects a
 non-positive width, emits a "Margin is wider than the output width" warning
 via whine(), and falls back to a zero margin with the full output width so
 that wrapping can always make progress.
 .
 The upstream regression snippet (t/data/snippets/text/wrap-width) and its
 registration in t/text/snippets.t are intentionally omitted from this
 backport.  The newly added data file is not present in the podlators MANIFEST
 that the Debian perl build uses to populate its build/test tree, so the file
 is never copied into build-shared and the snippet test aborts with
 "cannot open t/data/snippets/text/wrap-width: No such file or directory".
 The functional security fix in the four modules is unaffected.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/a0af540403eb609b5f3a6dfefd8561eb8d7484cd
Author: Russ Allbery <rra@cpan.org>
Last-Update: 2026-09-23
---
--- a/cpan/podlators/lib/Pod/Text.pm
+++ b/cpan/podlators/lib/Pod/Text.pm
@@ -253,6 +253,17 @@ sub wrap {
     my $output = '';
     my $spaces = ' ' x $$self{MARGIN};
     my $width = $$self{opt_width} - $$self{MARGIN};
+
+    # Pathological margins make wrapping impossible.  In this case, complain
+    # to the user and reset the margin to 0.
+    if ($width <= 0) {
+        my $error = 'Margin is wider than the output width';
+        $self->whine($self->line_count(), $error);
+        $spaces = q{};
+        $width = $self->{opt_width};
+    }
+
+    # Perform the wrapping.
     while (length > $width) {
         if (s/^([^\n]{0,$width})[ \t\n]+// || s/^([^\n]{$width})//) {
             $output .= $spaces . $1 . "\n";
